//? Title: Mask R-CNN aligned regions and individual masks
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An object detector supplies boxes,but separating each object's pixels also requires accurate spatial alignment and a class-specific support prediction. This report checks aligned tensor sampling and mask gradients,then visibly fits every branch of the source compact Mask R-CNN and plots real held-out masks and measured errors.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/mask_rcnn.cpp`.

> The method

Continuous regions supply aligned features to separate box and sigmoid mask heads. A shared backbone and RPN learn proposals jointly with classification,box regression and positive-region mask BCE. Tensor-generated MNIST scenes retain a separate support for every object.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/mask_rcnn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/mask_rcnn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/mask_rcnn_concept.tikz > build/mask_rcnn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/mask_rcnn_concept.svg build/mask_rcnn_concept.dvi > build/mask_rcnn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
