> Aligned sampling before classification

Mask R-CNN needs a separate binary support for each detected object. Quantizing
region boundaries can discard subpixel alignment,so this example retains
continuous pixel coordinates. A feature cell centre lies at image coordinate
\(s(i+1/2)\). For output bin \(j\) and sample \(a\in\{0,1\}\),the aligned
feature coordinate is

$$u_{j,a}=\frac{b_0+(j+(a+1/2)/2)(b_1-b_0)/B}{s}-\frac12.$$
\alttext(Each output bin averages two regularly spaced samples per axis,converted from pixel coordinates to the feature grid with a half-pixel shift.)

Four bilinear samples per bin are averaged,with border replication. This is
the source example's fixed regular2x2 aligned convention;it is not a claim that
every Mask R-CNN implementation uses the same alignment/default sampling ratio.
Boxes and image IDs are detached;gradients flow into features. The controlled
plane below has value \(1+2y+3x\),so interior bilinear interpolation reproduces
the plane exactly. Native independent arithmetic also checks every feature
derivative at fractional coordinates and replicated borders(error below3e-6).

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mask_rcnn_align.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  auto f = (1. + 2. * n::arange(0, 5).reshape({5, 1}) + 3. * n::arange(0, 5).reshape({1, 5}))
               .reshape({1, 5, 5, 1})
               .requires_grad_();
  const auto y = m::MaskRoiAlign(f, n::tensor({2., 2., 18., 18.}, {1, 4}),
                                 n::zeros({1}, n::DType::Int64), 4, 3);
  const auto g = n::grad(n::sum(y), {f})[0];
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(f.reshape({5, 5}), {0}), 0, 21),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(y.reshape({3, 3}), {0}), 0, 21),
       c = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(g.reshape({5, 5}), {0}), 0, 1.5);
  const auto expected = 1. + (8. / 3.) * (n::arange(0, 3).reshape({3, 1}) + .5) +
                        4. * (n::arange(0, 3).reshape({1, 3}) + .5);
  const auto difference = y.reshape({3, 3}) - expected;
  if (n::max(n::abs(difference)).item() > 1e-5)
    return 1;
  auto d = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(difference, {0}), -1e-5, 1e-5);
  d.title("Output minus affine oracle");
  a.title("Input affine feature plane");
  b.title("Aligned three-bin output");
  c.title("Feature derivative footprint");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 2)
      .add(a)
      .add(b)
      .add(c)
      .add(d)
      .size(1100, 900)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/mask_rcnn_align.svg");
  std::print("Aligned first/centre/last values:{:.6f}/{:.6f}/{:.6f};feature gradient "
             "sum:{:.6f} for nine outputs. Boxes detached,no fitting.\n",
             y.to_vector<float>()[0], y.to_vector<float>()[4], y.to_vector<float>()[8],
             n::sum(g).item());
  if (std::abs(n::sum(g).item() - 9) > 1e-6)
    return 1;
}
```
