> The initialized full mask head and the complete compact model

The full mask branch uses four256-channel3x3 ReLU convolutions,a learned2x2
stride2 transpose convolution and80 linear class channels. It has2,643,280
learned scalars and twelve parameter tensors;the complete initialized head and
all gradients execute below. This checks the mask branch,not a complete
pretrained ResNet/FPN Mask R-CNN.

The fitted source adaptation uses a64px grayscale stride4 backbone,a hidden128
RPN with2304 anchors,an aligned7-bin hidden256 box head,and an aligned14-bin
mask head with four32-channel layers and ten28x28 mask channels. Every branch
is trained. There is no BN or moving model state.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  for (bool full : {true, false}) {
    n::ParameterStore p(17);
    const int channels = full ? 256 : 64;
    const auto input =
        n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 2 * 14 * 14 * channels)).reshape({2, 14, 14, channels});
    const auto output = m::MaskRcnnHead(p, input, full ? 256 : 32, full ? 80 : 10);
    const auto g = n::grad(n::mean(n::square(output)), p.parameters());
    for (const auto &value : g)
      if (!value.defined() ||
          !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(value.to(n::DType::Float64))).item()) ||
          (!full && n::sum(n::square(value)).item() <= 0))
        return 1;
    if (p.count() != (full ? 2643280 : 50666) || g.size() != 12)
      return 1;
    std::print(
        "{} mask head:{} learned scalars,{} finite gradients,28px output;no fitted weights.\n",
        full ? "Full" : "Compact", p.count(), g.size());
  }
}
```
